# These two files are copied verbatim into an isolated Linux environment, so they
# must carry LF on every platform, including a Windows checkout.
#
# The repository default is `* text=auto`, and `*.py` is declared text without an
# eol, so both would arrive as CRLF here. A CRLF in the wrapper's shebang makes it
# unexecutable on Linux, and the error says nothing useful about why.
#
# The wrapper has no extension, so no other rule in the root .gitattributes reaches
# it — `*.sh text eol=lf` does not apply.
mcp-bridge.py       text eol=lf
iped-mcp-bridge     text eol=lf
